# Citation metadata for this collection.
#
# This file and `.zenodo.json` describe the same release. Keep the title, the
# author list, the version and the licence identical in both.
#
# The licence is decided. Marc Erhardt chose it on 15 August 2026.
# `GPL-3.0-only` covers the collection's own code, which is what this software
# record describes. It replaces the MIT licence chosen earlier on the same day.
# It does not cover the vendored trees under `models/*/upstream/` (they keep
# their own licences), or the documentation, figures and data deposit
# (CC-BY-4.0). CFF 1.2.0 holds one identifier per record, so `LICENSES.md`
# carries the per-directory map and is the authority.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS — resolve before the release is published:
#   * repository-code / url — set 15 August 2026.
#   * version — must equal the git tag and the version in `.zenodo.json`
#     and `pyproject.toml`.
#   * date-released — add the real release date (see the commented key below).
#   * ORCIDs — only Michael Jahn's ORCID could be verified inside this
#     repository. Every other author has no `orcid` key. Do not guess one:
#     CFF requires the exact form `https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000`, and
#     a wrong identifier points at a different person.
#   * identifiers / preferred-citation — add the Zenodo DOI and the manuscript
#     citation once they exist. Templates are at the end of this file.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this collection, please cite both the associated manuscript and
  this archived software release.
title: >-
  Reproducible analyses and figures for "The cost-benefit trade-off of
  peritrichous flagellation in bacteria"
abstract: >-
  This collection rebuilds every figure of the flagellar-number cost-benefit
  manuscript from registered input tables with recorded provenance. It covers
  the 12 August 2026 revision: seven main figures, five supplementary figures
  and 60 panels. Each panel has one canonical producer script, one output
  directory and one provenance document that names its inputs, its software and
  its random seeds. Reproduction is partial by design and the collection records
  the limits of each panel in machine-readable form.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
# date-released: YYYY-MM-DD   # uncomment and set on the day of the release
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/SalmoLab/salmonella-flagella-cost-benefit
url: https://github.com/SalmoLab/salmonella-flagella-cost-benefit

